{
  "$comment": "NEW. For a learner who cannot read, the icon IS the label — so an icon that means two things is a bug of the same severity as a mistranslation. This is a CLOSED set: adding an icon is a design decision made once, by Dev C, and recorded here. Style: single-weight line art, 2 dp stroke, no colour carrying meaning, drawn from the same visual world as the book's own illustrations (adult, Beninese, uncluttered) — never a children's icon set.",
  "rules": [
    "one icon, one meaning, app-wide",
    "an icon never carries meaning by colour alone (§J.3)",
    "every icon has a spoken label reachable by long-press",
    "minimum rendered size 32 dp inside a 56 dp target",
    "no emoji, ever — they render differently per device and read as childish"
  ],
